WEBVTT

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:17.140
I have born witness to
the business pursuits

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.780
this foundation has undertaken.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.480
There is but one thing
we hope to achieve:

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.040
the further evolution of mankind.

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:29.510
Humans have yet to awaken
to their hidden potential.

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:32.550
When the chrysalis takes
flight as a butterfly,

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:36.110
there will be no war, no famine,

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:39.000
no discrimination, no borders.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:41.220
Realizing this perfect world

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.680
should definitely be in our power.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.720
For the sake of that brilliant future,

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:48.940
we shall exert all our efforts.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.450
I make you all this promise:

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:58.530
The Loewenherz Foundation
shall construct Heaven on Earth.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:20.850
Lost

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:23.970
Tesaguri de sagashiteta
I've searched, groping

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:27.900
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
The answer to a future that's been closed off

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:29.810
Tozasareta mirai no kotae nante doko nimo nai
Is nowhere to be found

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:33.150
Hashiru shoudou, ima kaidoku funou
The impulse to run, it's impossible to decipher now

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.860
Found

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:39.110
Kudaketa hazu no unmei o
A fate that was supposedly smashed

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:43.580
Mijuku na yume no naka de kikoeta kitanda
I've come to hear it within that half-formed dream:

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:46.410
Saigo made I'll be there for you
Until the end, I'll be there for you

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:49.500
Tachidomaranai, kono hari dake wa
It won't stop, not this needle

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.840
Boku no asu o kizamu oto o tsukisasu
It will pierce the sound that engraves my tomorrow

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:54.760
Shinjitsu kara nigetara ima
If I run from the truth, then now...

00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:56.470
Genjitsu ni mo maketara ima
If I lose to reality, then now...

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:58.800
Nani ga nokoru no?
What will remain?

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.010
(Nokoru no?)
(Will remain?)

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.390
Kazoekirenai kono kizu dake ga
These countless wounds of mine

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:06.850
Boku no kinou o zanzou to shite kataru
They tell of my yesterday as an afterimage

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:08.560
Unmei ga hodoketemo ima
Even if fate were unraveled, now...

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:10.400
Sonzai o kowashitemo ima
Even if my existence were smashed, now...

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:13.270
Boku no michi o yuku yo
I will travel my path

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:15.400
It's now or never

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:16.490
That is what they say

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:18.570
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:22.240
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.410
That is what they say

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:25.580
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:29.080
There will always be,
there will always be a way

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:30.290
That is what they say

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:32.710
Live your life today, yeah, yeah

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:39.010
The Ruler Atop the Board

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:45.380
An excellent speech, Mr. Klondike.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:50.560
Such nonsense befits
those of their stature.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:53.310
Say, Uncle,

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.780
isn't there anything
interesting going on?

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:59.130
Since we've stopped being friends
with the Orpheus Order,

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:01.140
I've been so bored!

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:03.050
My apologies.

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.870
We still have yet to discover
Freecell's whereabouts.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:08.370
There's nothing to worry about.

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:09.790
Oh, my!

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:11.770
This is...

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:12.570
Freecell!

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:14.880
Mr. Klondike, you have him?

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:20.470
I shall allow no one to attempt to
evade my calculations.

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:22.220
Then you have already...

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:26.350
Thanks to the final data
extracted from his Ring...

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:29.220
The Final Ring has been completed.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:33.020
Everything is going according
to my calculations.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:34.240
Sir.

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:37.270
Melancholy, please get things ready.

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:39.150
We're going to go play somewhere?

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:42.570
Yes, to begin the ceremony.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:51.750
Jeez, where did Doubt
and Pinochle run off to?

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:55.480
The POG was giving them protection,

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:58.130
so for them to disappear
without saying anything...

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:01.530
I just don't like those guys!

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:05.010
I, Ana, think Gammon seems lonely!

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.740
I..I ain't lonely at all!

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:10.700
Still, Mizerka has been saved

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:12.810
and we've basically won the fight

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:14.980
against the Orpheus Order, right?

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:19.880
No, details of their
organization remain unclear.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:20.700
Especially...

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:22.310
Klondike.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:24.890
The one who gave Freecell and the

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:27.200
others Replica Rings and
then controlled them...

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.010
He's the ringleader.

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:31.500
That guy hasn't shown his face at all.

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:35.460
Doubt said they didn't
know anything about him.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:37.210
Klondike...

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:39.200
Just who is he?

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:42.010
What?

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:47.930
This is...

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:50.600
The emergency partitions
have lowered on their own!

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.270
External communications
are completely cut off!

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:56.650
Who could do something like this?

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:03.790
Oh, Kaito, let's play!

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:13.910
What do you all think you're doing?!

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:18.110
You're pickin' a fight
with the POG this time?!

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:20.750
Oh my, could you please
not get the wrong idea?

00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:25.320
I could have done that
any time I'd wanted to.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:29.140
It just happened to have
been today, that's all.

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:33.460
Miss Melancholy's prank
seems to have gone too far.

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:35.270
My apologies.

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:37.040
Today,

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:38.920
we have brought a message from

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:41.980
Mr. Klondike, Leader
of the Orpheus Order.

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:43.980
Klondike you say?!

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:48.880
Hello, Kaito Daimon.

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:50.950
I am Klondike.

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:54.440
I would like to offer you a game.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:56.410
A game?

00:05:56.690 --> 00:06:00.580
Perhaps by now you've thought
you'd like to see me?

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:03.990
If so, why not engage me in battle

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:05.990
that we may settle this,

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:08.700
via the puzzles you love so much?

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:10.160
Gimme a damn break!

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:11.700
That's right, he can't-

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:15.480
He can't just accept such
a one-sided proposition.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:17.730
That's what you're thinking.

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:21.530
However, perhaps Kaito has found himself

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:23.320
somewhat amenable to the idea.

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:27.070
Now then, allow me to
give one final push:

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:31.490
As of now, Freecell is in my keeping.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:32.740
What?!

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:35.240
I thought you wished to free him

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.710
from the Ring, save him, as it were.

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:38.460
Still...

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:43.570
You're free to choose
whether you believe or not.

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:47.170
I have prepared a suitable
setting for our game.

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:53.450
I shall guide you.

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:01.880
Hey, is this really all right?

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:03.310
It could be a trap.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.420
We don't have a choice.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:07.920
He says he has Freecell.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:10.200
But that could just be a lie!

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:14.740
I, Ana, think it doesn't
matter if it's true or a lie.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:17.840
You think that idiot could do nothing

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:20.490
after bein' told something like that?

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:24.290
That bastard Klondike
is a hell of a schemer.

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:27.320
No matter what awaits me,

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:29.610
I'll take it on and I'll win!

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:38.210
How far do they plan on takin' us?

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:40.310
Ah, there!

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:51.070
It's...

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:55.910
You must be tired after your long journey,
Kaito Daimon.

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:59.660
Klondike, where is Freecell?!

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:04.350
I will tell you once you've beaten me.

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:06.190
You're fulla crap!

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:07.710
Who do you think you are?!

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:12.470
Who do you think you are
addressing, peasant?

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:15.920
Do you still not understand?

00:08:16.660 --> 00:08:19.950
I have already provided for you.

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:22.380
You have a chance at a game

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:24.430
you would otherwise not survive.

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:29.100
Ascend, I shall be your opponent.

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:41.060
That bastard Klondike...

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:44.390
How come he's gotten all bold and
wants to pick a fight now?

00:08:44.390 --> 00:08:46.770
So, could he have some other objective?

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:48.930
I, Ana, think...

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:51.050
That man is completely dark.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:53.050
I can see nothing.

00:08:53.490 --> 00:08:57.320
I'll doing some digging,
find out who he is!

00:08:57.320 --> 00:08:59.030
Well, Uncle...

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:00.910
I hope you'll let us enjoy this.

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:05.190
Do you even get it?

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:10.070
This Klondike person is
manipulating you too!

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:14.380
Listen, Mizerka and Doubt's Rings were-

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:19.070
You're the one who doesn't get it.

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:22.330
I'm different from those guys.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:23.080
Huh?

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:25.810
Look, it's starting.

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:32.110
This game is a match-style maze puzzle,
the Straying Field.

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:36.850
First, you must draw a maze
within a 20 x 20 field.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:40.580
However, your opponent will be unable
to see the maze's walls.

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:42.910
You must each solve this unseen maze.

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:45.120
That is the objective of this game.

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:48.240
Both players, please
make mazes with the goal

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:50.280
being your opponent's current position.

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:53.320
Making and solving...

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:58.950
A puzzle that tests abilities
as both Giver and Solver, huh?

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:01.950
The fight's already begun!

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:09.210
Still, they were most
foolish, weren't they?

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:11.230
Doubt and the others?

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:12.230
Huh?

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:14.320
They believed till the end, yes?

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:17.250
That the Rings were being developed

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:19.180
to be shared with all mankind.

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:23.140
It was all a lie.

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:24.560
What?

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:26.210
It can't be!

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:27.560
Then why?!

00:10:28.170 --> 00:10:30.900
If you present them with ideals,

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:33.990
you can use any number of fools.

00:10:33.990 --> 00:10:36.110
The true purpose was none other than...

00:10:36.810 --> 00:10:41.700
to create the one Final Ring for myself.

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:43.620
Final Ring?!

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:48.060
All have acted according
to my calculations.

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:49.270
Freecell...

00:10:49.850 --> 00:10:53.130
And Kaito Daimon, you as well.

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:56.780
I have repeated experiments throughout

00:10:56.780 --> 00:10:59.960
the world to complete the Ring.

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:01.020
However...

00:11:01.490 --> 00:11:04.820
No specimen has provided me with such

00:11:04.820 --> 00:11:06.640
excellent data as yourself.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:10.420
Bastard, you've gone too far!

00:11:10.420 --> 00:11:11.420
That's right!

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:12.980
How can you do this to people?!

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:15.380
The fates of Freecell and the

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:18.400
others were screwed up
for the likes of you?!

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:20.820
I'm grateful.

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:22.400
You're goin' down.

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:27.330
There's no way I'm lettin'
you pull off this plan!

00:11:31.730 --> 00:11:34.020
It seems your maze
preparations are complete.

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:36.500
Mr. Kaito, you go first.

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.010
Now then, shall we begin?

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:44.260
It's the ceremony of awakening!

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:53.200
That guy has a Replica Ring too?

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:58.190
Oh my, Uncle's Ring isn't some replica.

00:11:58.590 --> 00:12:01.740
That's none other than the Final Ring!

00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:04.200
Now then, the Straying Field...

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:05.420
Play.

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:12.250
Here I come!

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:16.610
Both players may progress
through the field.

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:23.420
When you hit a wall, movement halts

00:12:23.420 --> 00:12:25.390
and the other player takes a turn.

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:30.390
Also, the first player
to reach his goal wins.

00:12:41.510 --> 00:12:43.880
If you just go by trial and error,

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:45.530
you'll never reach the goal.

00:12:46.010 --> 00:12:48.320
You've gotta read the opponent's maze,

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:49.750
infer the entire layout.

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:53.160
This is a super high-level puzzle!

00:13:21.880 --> 00:13:23.320
Kaito's havin' a tough time of it.

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:24.970
No way...

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:26.180
It's to be expected.

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:27.570
Having to avoid walls you can't see,

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:29.780
moving forward with no hints...

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:31.830
It would take unbelievable skill to read

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:34.330
the opponent's thought process that quickly.

00:13:37.430 --> 00:13:40.580
I see, so this is your maze, eh?

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:45.230
What's goin' on?

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:47.840
I can't read his maze at all!

00:13:48.340 --> 00:13:52.240
What's more, I don't feel
anything from his maze!

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:55.370
What is this blank-faced maze?!

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:58.350
I should have told you at the start:

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:02.070
There is absolutely no
way you can beat me.

00:14:02.710 --> 00:14:05.510
Such was the outcome of my calculations.

00:14:05.510 --> 00:14:06.530
Shut up!

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:09.280
That reaction follows my calculations.

00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:11.140
Calculations, calculations!

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:12.270
Shut up already!

00:14:19.610 --> 00:14:21.360
This is a puzzle.

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:23.550
It is nothing more than a foolish game.

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:25.300
What was that?

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:26.590
My apologies.

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:30.970
Today was actually my first
time to play a puzzle.

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:35.230
To me, this puzzle is nothing more

00:14:35.230 --> 00:14:37.480
than a means to achieve my goal.

00:14:37.830 --> 00:14:42.690
Yes, like you, Freecell and
the rest, it is just a tool.

00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:48.300
So, that guy's an amateur at puzzles?!

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:51.050
How can he do it faster than Kaito?

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:52.480
Don't tell me,

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:56.000
that's the power of
this Final Ring thing!

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:56.870
No!

00:14:57.680 --> 00:14:59.900
This isn't the Ring's power.

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:02.670
His Ring isn't active yet.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.070
What was that?!

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:07.470
Klondike is fighting
with his own abilities.

00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:09.980
Impossible!

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:13.910
You're sayin' he's already
better than Kaito?!

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:17.530
I, Ana, think that if
his Ring goes active...

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:19.480
This is really bad.

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:24.360
If that's the case, what is
the meaning of this game?

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:36.490
Serves you right, Kaito Daimon!

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:39.870
Uncle, please be even meaner to him!

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:42.370
Shut your ass up there!

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:45.680
Two-bit fakes wearing fake-ass Rings

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:47.050
can shut their pieholes!

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:49.260
I believe I told you:

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:52.340
I am not like the others.

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:56.100
Ah, what is this?!

00:15:56.660 --> 00:15:58.450
What's wrong, Cube?

00:15:58.450 --> 00:15:59.910
I get it now.

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:01.890
Compared to the data
from the last battle,

00:16:01.890 --> 00:16:03.750
that Ring's reading just now...

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:05.900
It's not a Replica Ring!

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:08.090
Do you understand now?

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:10.400
I am the real thing.

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:12.280
"Real thing"?

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:16.410
It's like sitting on a gold
mine, in the truest sense.

00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:18.100
What does that mean?

00:16:18.650 --> 00:16:22.860
What Miss Melancholy wears
is a real Orpheus Ring.

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:28.920
And she herself is a
true Phi-Brain child.

00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:37.240
Mr. Klondike acquired
the real Orpheus Ring,

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:40.060
which was previously stored
by the Orpheus Order.

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:45.080
But the one the Ring chose wasn't me.

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:46.560
It was Melancholy.

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:48.300
However,

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:53.360
Melancholy had no aspirations
of becoming a Phi-Brain.

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:58.320
I mean, all this Phi-Brain and
Puzzle of God stuff

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:00.340
is a big pain.

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:04.370
I'm fine being able to
just have fun and play.

00:17:05.400 --> 00:17:07.840
That's why you made the Replica Rings!

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:11.820
Yes, to obtain the
power of the Phi-Brain,

00:17:11.820 --> 00:17:14.840
it was necessary to complete
them, no matter what.

00:17:15.490 --> 00:17:18.970
Additionally, I made use
of the Orpheus Order.

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:23.910
I used the great cause
of "freeing mankind,"

00:17:23.910 --> 00:17:28.580
to complete the one, sole
Final Ring for myself.

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:31.750
What I want...

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:36.310
is the intellect to calculate
and control all events

00:17:36.310 --> 00:17:37.820
within this world.

00:17:39.230 --> 00:17:42.120
At the dawn of my becoming a Phi-Brain,

00:17:42.670 --> 00:17:45.540
all that happens in this world

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:48.790
shall rest in the palm of my hand.

00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:50.650
Shut the hell up!

00:17:50.650 --> 00:17:53.110
You're tryin' to become
God or somethin'?!

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:54.280
God?

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:57.180
I've never once believed
such a thing exists.

00:17:57.610 --> 00:18:01.160
However, once I've acquired this power,

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:02.850
people will no doubt...

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:04.390
call me "God"!

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:07.500
That ain't gonna happen!

00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:08.770
"Calculations," my ass!

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:11.640
I'm gonna smash your
calculations to hell!

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:14.800
Right here, right now!

00:18:29.470 --> 00:18:32.750
Kaito Daimon, just as I've calculated...

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:34.720
You've lost.

00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:37.050
Shut the hell up.

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:40.550
There ain't no puzzle I can't solve!

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:50.380
Something's weird about this maze.

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:53.280
If all the walls I've hit
so far are connected,

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:57.320
it makes a closed-off area, not a maze.

00:18:58.430 --> 00:18:59.070
Don't tell me...

00:19:09.610 --> 00:19:10.790
I knew it!

00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:18.110
Right from the start,
this wasn't a maze!

00:19:18.110 --> 00:19:20.550
He just arranged walls
separate from one another!

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:24.720
I've figured out your puzzle!

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:33.480
Honestly, you act per my
calculations, Kaito Daimon.

00:19:40.510 --> 00:19:41.970
You've done it, Kaito!

00:19:41.970 --> 00:19:43.930
Go all the way to the goal!

00:19:43.930 --> 00:19:44.830
No!

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:48.060
No, Kaito...

00:19:48.520 --> 00:19:50.490
Don't solve the puzzle!

00:19:52.940 --> 00:19:55.000
I know it, this puzzle.

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:56.990
I win!

00:19:58.170 --> 00:20:00.470
I've waited for that.

00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:12.390
What's happening?

00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:14.230
I don't know,

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:17.070
it's like the field is intensifying somehow.

00:20:29.350 --> 00:20:30.080
It can't be!

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:33.330
The Final Ring is activated!

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:35.210
I see it...

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:36.090
I can see it!

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:39.280
Via Kaito Daimon's data,

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:40.880
all the puzzle answers up till now.

00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:43.520
This is the Ring's power?

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:47.890
As I calculated, the Ring's
awakening was a success!

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:51.610
Uncle, you've finally become one,

00:20:52.370 --> 00:20:53.640
a Phi-Brain.

00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:57.280
Bastard, just what have you done?

00:20:57.920 --> 00:21:01.400
Activating the Final
Ring, Mr. Kaito Daimon,

00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:04.440
required the limitless
power of one such as you,

00:21:04.440 --> 00:21:07.230
who had approached Phi-Brain potential.

00:21:07.230 --> 00:21:12.080
This field was a device
for amplifying your power.

00:21:12.780 --> 00:21:15.790
That power was the
priming agent, and now,

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:18.510
the Final Ring has been awakened.

00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:22.420
The game ends here.

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:25.350
I'm grateful to you, Kaito Daimon.

00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:28.850
Without you,
the Ring could not have been awakened.

00:21:32.080 --> 00:21:34.770
Klondike, you prick!

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:38.190
Now then, let's go, Melancholy.

00:21:38.540 --> 00:21:39.990
Okay, Uncle.

00:21:40.550 --> 00:21:41.940
Wait there, Klondike!

00:21:43.220 --> 00:21:44.550
Freecell...

00:21:44.550 --> 00:21:46.200
Where's Freecell?

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:48.810
Ah, him, eh?

00:21:52.550 --> 00:21:53.420
Freecell!

00:21:54.270 --> 00:21:58.900
I used him as sacrifice
for completing the Ring.

00:21:58.900 --> 00:22:01.050
The shock of extracting his data

00:22:01.560 --> 00:22:03.850
caused him to lose consciousness.

00:22:17.120 --> 00:22:17.770
Freecell...

00:22:18.830 --> 00:22:21.840
Freecell!

00:22:25.550 --> 00:22:26.550
Kaito...

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:40.050
Eiyuukidori
Playing the hero

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:44.940
Itsudatte shinjita muteki no kankaku
A sense of invincibility you always believed in

00:22:45.550 --> 00:22:51.370
Tatakatte iru no wa chikyuu no tame nanka ja nai
You're not fighting for the sake of the world or anything

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:54.160
Motto maipeesu de
It's for a more leisurely

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:59.230
Sou, motto shoujiki na onegai no tame
Yeah, more straightforward request

00:22:59.600 --> 00:23:07.670
Nandotonaku kizutsuitemo tachiagare, hero
Even if you're wounded over and over, rise up, hero

00:23:07.670 --> 00:23:13.220
Kitto daijoubu, kimi o mamorunda
It's sure to be all right, I'll protect you

00:23:13.610 --> 00:23:17.040
Machigai da to shitemo tomarenai
Even if it's wrong, it can't be stopped

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:20.650
Seikai ka nante wakaranai
I don't know if it's the right answer

00:23:21.550 --> 00:23:24.660
Donna toki demo original ni
No matter the situation

00:23:24.660 --> 00:23:27.400
Step o fumidashiteku
I'll take those first steps, originally

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:30.770
Dramatic ni, mawaru sekai de
On this spinning world, I'm searching, dramatically

00:23:30.770 --> 00:23:34.430
Kiwameita wonder sagashiteru
For wonders that sparkle

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:38.430
Boku, shijou saikou no tabi o tsuzukeyou
Me, I'll keep going on the greatest journey in history

00:23:38.430 --> 00:23:42.740
Image shite shiawase na mirai e
To the happy future I imagined

00:23:44.430 --> 00:23:46.060
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:51.380
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:52.800
Mirai e
To the future

00:23:54.710 --> 00:23:56.260
(Mirai e)
(To the future)

00:24:02.520 --> 00:24:04.490
Klondike of the Orpheus Order decides to

00:24:04.490 --> 00:24:06.560
rely on a "Tanaka" from Kanagawa.

00:24:07.150 --> 00:24:09.700
He writes a love letter
inside a crossword puzzle,

00:24:09.700 --> 00:24:12.360
but come the appointed meeting time,
the girl fails to show.

00:24:12.360 --> 00:24:14.680
"Will springtime come for me?"

00:24:14.680 --> 00:24:16.290
Sorry, Tanaka!

00:24:16.290 --> 00:24:17.790
That was too bad, huh?

00:24:17.790 --> 00:24:20.110
A letter would have been
easier to understand.

00:24:20.110 --> 00:24:22.210
Next time, "God's Miscalculation"

00:24:21.580 --> 00:24:26.670
God's Miscalculation

00:24:22.210 --> 00:24:24.540
I shall be counting on you.
